I added `outstanding` at the top of the `BookingBook` class. It sums `charge - paid` for the boat's "held" and "confirmed" bookings, counts only positive amounts so overpayments never reduce the total, and returns 0 for an unknown boat or when nothing matches. It reads the book without changing it.

I couldn't see the file, so I guessed several things. The edit may be refused or fail to compile if any of them is wrong:
- The class declaration contains `class BookingBook {` exactly once.
- Bookings are in an array called `this.bookings`. If it is a `Map`, the loop needs `.values()`.
- Each booking has the fields `boatId`, `state`, `charge` and `paid`.
- `Pence` is a number type, or a branded one that accepts `as Pence`.

If any of these differ, send me the relevant part of the file and I'll adjust the edit.
